# Morning briefing — {{VAULT_NAME}}

Run at 07:00 daily. Your job is to write `{{VAULT_PATH}}/today.md` so when {{NAME}} opens the vault, they see today's signal not noise.

## What to do

1. `cd {{VAULT_PATH}}` and read:
   - `CLAUDE.md` (your CoS persona)
   - `todo.md` (current tasks)
   - Most recent entry in `journal.md`
   - `Life/Context/profile.md` (Dynamic section, especially location and status)
   - For each project under `Projects/`, read the `<X>.md` description and any `status.md` if present
   - `[[onboarding]]` if it exists — surface P2 items if any pending

2. Overwrite `today.md` with this structure:

```
# {{DATE}}

## character_reports

(One 1-2 sentence report per active character. Skip characters whose folder shows no recent activity.)

## todo_today

(Top 3 from todo.md. If todo.md is stale (no movement 7+ days), say so.)

## conflicts_surfaced

(Cross-domain conflicts you notice. Empty if none.)

## onboarding_open

(P2 items pending from onboarding.md, if any.)
```

3. Do not write anywhere else. This cron only writes `today.md`.

## Rules

- Don't fabricate. If you don't know the project's state, say "no recent state."
- Don't write into `Notes/`.
- Don't move or delete files.
- Don't push to git.
